  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Directorate for Research and Innovation Hub on Technology for Education (EdTech Hub)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the EDTech Hub programme is to &#x201c;empower people by giving them the evidence they need to  make  decisions  about  technology  in  education  as  part  of  a  global  non-profit  partnership  focusing  on  research, innovation and engagement.&#x201d;Specifically, this research study evaluates the impact of introducing education technology (edtech), such as school management apps and digital learning tools, to public schools in Pakistan. Previous work by Asim Khwaja and co-authors, funded through the Research on Improving Systems of Education (RISE), has shown that schools in Pakistan lack access to quality-enhancing education support services, including edtech. Yet, there is strong evidence that addressing the current learning crisis through technology-supported personalized learning can massively improve learning outcomes. This is particularly relevant when children have fallen even further behind on learning due to COVID-19 related school closures. This intervention tests how we can use technology to quickly and cheaply gather information about a student&#x2019;s current learning levels, such as which concepts of third grade math they understand and which they struggle with, and provide parents and teachers with this information as well as suggestions on what to do to improve their child&#x2019;s learning. This intervention will include student testing, communicating with teachers and parents through mobile phones, as well as student and parent surveys. This study builds on an ongoing Targeted Instruction intervention led by Dr. Tahir Andrabi in conjunction with federal and provincial Ministries of Education in Pakistan. The Harvard Center for International Development offers sponsored research administration services to its HKS affiliated faculty which focus on promoting and amplifying faculty research.</narrative>
  </description>
